    <briefdescription>
<para>Contiguous data storage for <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> objects. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1tensor_1_1TensorStorage" kindref="compound">TensorStorage</ref> class is responsible for holding the raw data associated with a <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> object in a contiguous block of memory. <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1tensor_1_1TensorStorage" kindref="compound">TensorStorage</ref> objects are not intended to be interacted with directly, but rather through the <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> class which provides the primary interface for all tensor operations. The TensorView-TensorStorage structure is designed such that multiple <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> objects can share a single <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1tensor_1_1TensorStorage" kindref="compound">TensorStorage</ref> object, allowing for efficient memory usage when creating sub-tensor views or shallow copies of tensors.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> for the primary interface by which tensor objects are interacted with. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
